  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["punctuation.definition.comment.json","/*"]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0"],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["comment.block.json","\tOverview: "]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0"],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["comment.block.json","\tA system for tracking \"good and bad\" actions, and returning the proportion the player has encountered in the course of their playthrough. "]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0"],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["comment.block.json","\te.g. the player has said 15 nice things and 5 nasty things, so they are 75% nice."]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0"],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["comment.block.json","\tThis allows the game to make decisions about the balance of the player's choices across the game regardless of knowing how many choice moments they've actually encountered. "]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0"],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["comment.block.json","\tIt also means that the player's behaviour settles over time - each additional decision they take has less and less effect on the overall value. In short, \"what's done is done.\""]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0"],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0"],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["comment.block.json","\tSystem:"]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0"],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["comment.block.json","\tEach concept is given a \"swing variable\", which after being given an initial value, can be \"raised\" or \"lowered\"."]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0"],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["comment.block.json","\tFor more significant actions, one can \"elevate\" or \"ditch\" it. For all-but-irrecoverable actions, you can \"escalate\" or \"demolish\" the stat."]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0"],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["comment.block.json","\tTo test the variable, the following queries are provided: \"high\", \"up\", \"mid\", \"down\", \"low\"."]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0"],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["comment.block.json","\tNote that the system won't return a \"up\" or \"down\" result until the player has taken a few choices to seed the system."]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0"],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0"],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["comment.block.json","\tUsage:"]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0"],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["comment.block.json","\t// initialise the variable"]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["comment.block.json","\tVAR niceness = INITIAL_SWING"]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0"],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["comment.block.json","\t// alter the variable"]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["comment.block.json","\t~ raise(niceness) \t\t// note a nice choice"]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["comment.block.json","\t~ lower(niceness)\t\t// note a nasty choice "]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0"],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["comment.block.json","\t// test the variable"]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["comment.block.json","\tI'm <>"]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["comment.block.json","\t{ "]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["comment.block.json","\t- up(niceness):"]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["comment.block.json","\t\tnice "]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["comment.block.json","\t- down(niceness):"]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["comment.block.json","\t\tnasty "]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["comment.block.json","\t- else: "]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["comment.block.json","\t\tundecided "]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["comment.block.json","\t} "]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0",["comment.block.json","\t<>."]],
  ["punctuation.definition.comment.json0"],
